#/-------------------[DOTENV_PUBLIC_KEY]--------------------/
#/       versioned X25519 encryption for .env files         /
#/       [how it works](https://stacksjs.com/encryption)   /
#/----------------------------------------------------------/

# Secrets for the production environment.
#
# Values here are encrypted with the public key in this file and decrypted at
# deploy time with the matching private key, which is NOT committed. CI reads
# it from the DOTENV_PRIVATE_KEY_PRODUCTION repository secret; locally it lives
# in .env.keys. This file is committed - that is the point: the ciphertext is
# reviewable and diffable, and losing a laptop does not leak production.
#
# Add one with:
#   buddy env:set STRIPE_SECRET_KEY --stdin --env production
#
# Nothing was copied out of your .env: that file describes a laptop, and a
# server is not one.
#
# The keypair was replaced on 2026-11-01 because the private key for the
# previous one was lost. Sign in with Apple (APPLE_CLIENT_ID, APPLE_TEAM_ID,
# APPLE_KEY_ID, APPLE_PRIVATE_KEY, APPLE_REDIRECT_URL) was encrypted to that
# key and could not be recovered, so it is not configured: the Apple button
# stays hidden until those five are set again from the Apple Developer portal.

BLOB_LOCAL_ROOT="/var/www/reviewos-shared/blobs"

